"""Authentication config.

`auth()`/`guard()` resolve the **default guard** below; a guard's name *is* its driver —
`session` (cookie sessions), `local` (username/password against the DB), or `oidc` (an external
identity provider, configured under an `oidc` key). Register your own with
`GuardManager.extend(name, factory)`.

The bearer-token API flow that `arvel new <app> --auth` scaffolds does not go through a guard — its
routes issue and check personal access tokens directly via `arvel.auth.tokens` — so it needs no
config here.
"""

config = {
    "default_guard": "session",
    # "oidc": {"issuer": env("OIDC_ISSUER"), "client_id": env("OIDC_CLIENT_ID"), ...},
}
